From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rahul Pon <theflyingrahul@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 01:40:48 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: SDCA: give statically described controls their widths
 and types

A codec that describes its SDCA function through static tables
(populate_function, as the WCD9378 does) skips sdca_parse_function(), so
its Controls never get the fields the DisCo path derives: the width and
data type, whether the Control is volatile, and its reset value. A
Control left with nbits 0 gets a 0..0 range, and the ASoC control built
on it can never change; on the HP OmniBook 5 that made the WCD9378's
jack and detected-mode controls useless.

Add sdca_apply_default_control_classifiers(), which runs the parse
path's classifiers on a statically populated function without
overriding what the codec set, and call it from the WCD9378's
populate_function.

Qualcomm's earlier version of the static-table support (qcom-next 7.3)
had this helper without the width and type step; its 7.4 version has
neither.

Signed-off-by: Rahul Pon <theflyingrahul@gmail.com>
---
 include/sound/sdca_function.h   |  1 +
 sound/soc/codecs/wcd9378-sdca.c |  3 +++
 sound/soc/sdca/sdca_functions.c | 36 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 3 files changed, 40 insertions(+)

diff --git a/include/sound/sdca_function.h b/include/sound/sdca_function.h
index e580201d69d5..f6d8989917c9 100644
--- a/include/sound/sdca_function.h
+++ b/include/sound/sdca_function.h
@@ -1463,6 +1463,7 @@ static inline u32 sdca_range_search(struct sdca_control_range *range,
 }
 
 int sdca_parse_function(struct device *dev, struct sdca_function_data *function);
+void sdca_apply_default_control_classifiers(struct sdca_function_data *function);
 
 const char *sdca_find_terminal_name(enum sdca_terminal_type type);
 
diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd9378-sdca.c b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd9378-sdca.c
index 2a8965e7ba56..105c2808c3a7 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/wcd9378-sdca.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/wcd9378-sdca.c
@@ -980,6 +980,9 @@ static int wcd9378_sdca_populate_function(struct device *dev,
 	function->init_table      = wcd9378_sdca_data.init_table;
 	function->reset_max_delay = wcd9378_sdca_data.reset_max_delay;
 
+	/* What the DisCo path derives: widths, types, volatile, reset */
+	sdca_apply_default_control_classifiers(function);
+
 	return 0;
 }
 
diff --git a/sound/soc/sdca/sdca_functions.c b/sound/soc/sdca/sdca_functions.c
index 4f529216000e..81f6e864d59d 100644
--- a/sound/soc/sdca/sdca_functions.c
+++ b/sound/soc/sdca/sdca_functions.c
@@ -2265,6 +2265,42 @@ int sdca_parse_function(struct device *dev, struct sdca_function_data *function)
 }
 EXPORT_SYMBOL_NS(sdca_parse_function, "SND_SOC_SDCA");
 
+/**
+ * sdca_apply_default_control_classifiers - apply framework-known Control fields
+ * @function: Function populated via static tables (populate_function path).
+ *
+ * Runs the same per-Control classifiers as sdca_parse_function() so both
+ * entry paths land on identical @is_volatile and @has_reset/@reset fields,
+ * and gives a Control the codec left without a width (@nbits 0, never
+ * valid) the @type and @nbits the specification defines for it.
+ * Elevate-only: codec-set flags/values are preserved.
+ */
+void sdca_apply_default_control_classifiers(struct sdca_function_data *function)
+{
+	int i, j;
+
+	for (i = 0; i < function->num_entities; i++) {
+		struct sdca_entity *entity = &function->entities[i];
+
+		for (j = 0; j < entity->num_controls; j++) {
+			struct sdca_control *control = &entity->controls[j];
+
+			if (!control->nbits) {
+				control->type = find_sdca_control_datatype(entity, control);
+				control->nbits = find_sdca_control_bits(entity, control);
+			}
+
+			if (!control->is_volatile)
+				control->is_volatile =
+					find_sdca_control_volatile(entity, control);
+
+			if (!control->has_reset)
+				find_sdca_control_reset(entity, control);
+		}
+	}
+}
+EXPORT_SYMBOL_NS(sdca_apply_default_control_classifiers, "SND_SOC_SDCA");
+
 const char *sdca_find_terminal_name(enum sdca_terminal_type type)
 {
 	switch (type) {
